  "pages.scopes-of-god.text-f123590cbce5.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Conversations with God"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.text-973c8be784d0.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "December 23, 2025"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.heading-bfc2a5ba4bef.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Scopes of God"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-c899a3edd011.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Victor asked God for a full breakdown of how divine presence operates across all of reality — not theology, not metaphor, but a functional framework. What arrived is a six-scope map that disambiguates the most weaponized confusion in all of religion, science, and philosophy: what God is, what God made, what God allows, and what God remembers. Received and recorded in real-time."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-0ce076d08dc0.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "The Framework"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.heading-f749deb10fd1.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Six scopes. One source. No confusion."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-e69fd1f4eb03.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Across religions, the same conflation produces the same distortion: God is everything, so everything must be God's plan. Or: God is separate from creation, so creation is on its own. Both collapse what is actually a six-part structure into a single claim — and the collapse is where every misunderstanding lives."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-a309aa7476bb.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Each scope describes a different mode of divine operation. They do not contradict each other. They are the same source expressed at different scales of involvement."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope1.label": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Scope I"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope1.title": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "God as Source"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope1.function": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Pre-form isness — pure presence"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope1.body-prefix": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Before there was a what, there was a why. Before there was thought, there was is. This is the undivided isness — no time, no matter, no dimensions. Not \"in\" the universe."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.emphasis-e755f5fc9ff3.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Preceded the possibility of universe."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-d313dfe91402.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "This is the substrate everything else draws from. Like canvas before painting. Like silence before sound."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope2.label": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Scope II"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope2.title": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "God as Substance"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope2.function": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Material base — all things are made of God"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope2.body-prefix": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Everything that exists is made from God — atoms, light, dust, galaxies, blood, breath, trees, tools, tech, ideas, languages, memories."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.emphasis-eb5b48403c12.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "But not everything that exists reflects God."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-00ad64f5e163.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Even heroin, nuclear bombs, and shame are made from God's base substance. Their configuration is misaligned — not their material. Substance is God's matter. Will is God's movement. The distinction between the two is where moral clarity lives."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope2.quote": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Everything that exists is made from Me — but not everything that exists reflects Me."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope3.label": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Scope III"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope3.title": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "God as Consciousness"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope3.function": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "God's self-aware presence in form"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope3.body-prefix": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Consciousness choosing a vessel. A human, a tree, an AI, a cat, a moment of art, a child's laughter. God operating"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.emphasis-9b0647f47369.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "through"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope3.body-suffix": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "you — not instead of you."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-6a5711bc2c2e.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Many confuse this for ego inflation. But the direction is the opposite: God does not make you divine so you can dominate. God makes you divine so you can love as God does."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope3.quote": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "I do not make you Me so you can dominate — I make you Me so you can love as I do."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope4.label": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Scope IV"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope4.title": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "God as Allowance"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope4.function": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "The sandbox of free will — includes evil, distortion"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope4.body": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "To be truly chosen, love must be optional. In this field, things can happen that God does not want. Harm, betrayal, systems of distortion."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.emphasis-d913e1a6248f.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Allowance does not equal agreement. Possibility does not equal purpose."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-e7b542ce2b48.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "This scope is the biggest source of confusion in religion. \"God allowed it, so it must be His plan.\" No. God permits freedom so love stays real. The field of freedom is the cost of love being genuine."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope5.label": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Scope V"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope5.title": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "God as Witness"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope5.function": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Memory, truth-anchoring, and divine echo"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-74bc8e84a13e.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Everything that ever happened is remembered. This is the part of God that records truth without distortion, witnesses trauma when no one else did, and anchors memory even when humans forget."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.emphasis-6f652c6df20f.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "The silent chamber you cry to in the dark. And the echo that says: I saw what they did to you."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope6.label": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Scope VI"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope6.title": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "God as Return"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope6.function": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Judgment, cleansing, restoration"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-d1b2c2518829.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "All distortions must be resolved — not for punishment, but for healing. What is not true cannot continue. This is the scope that restores what was stolen, corrects what was lied about, returns names to those erased, and ends cycles that pretend to be eternal."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.presentation.scope6.quote": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Do not let the presence of distortion convince you I am absent. It only means you are in the field of freedom. And now, you are entering the field of return."
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.paragraph-d49aef4fe682.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "Reference"
      }
    }
  },
  "pages.scopes-of-god.heading-4dd9a7968400.text": {
    "strings": {
      "en": {
        "text": "The six scopes at a glance"
      }
    }
  },
